@startuml Mobile Operational Lifecycle and Revocation
autonumber
skinparam actorStyle AWESOME

skinparam BoxPadding 10

actor "Patient User" as User
participant "Flutter App Context" as App
participant "Secure Keystore" as Storage
participant "Nginx Gateway" as Nginx
participant "Node.js BFF" as BFF
participant "Redis Cache" as Redis
participant "HAPI FHIR Server" as FHIR
participant "Keycloak IdP" as KC

== 1. API Call with Runtime Token Verification ==
User -> App : Action requiring Record Aqcuisition
App -> Storage : Fetch Access Token
Storage --> App : Present Token String Payload

alt Token Check Indicates Local Expiration
    App -> Storage : Pull Active Long-Lived Refresh Token
    App -> KC : POST /protocol/openid-connect/token (Refresh Grant)
    KC --> App : Yield Fresh Token Payload
    App -> Storage : Commit Refreshed Assets to Keystore
end

App -> Nginx : GET needed api endpoint
Nginx -> BFF : Forward Request with Bearer Token
BFF -> BFF : Parse User Identity

alt Target Cache Match Valid
    BFF -> Redis : Query Clinical Cache Store
    Redis --> BFF : Return Cached PHI Context
else Cache Miss
    BFF -> FHIR : Query Patient data
    activate FHIR
    FHIR --> BFF : Return Data
    deactivate FHIR
    BFF -> Redis : Write Data to Cache
end

BFF --> Nginx : Return Payload
Nginx --> App : Forward Payload Response
App -> User : Render Content on the Display

== 2. Local-First Per-Session Sign Out ==
User -> App : Tap "Sign Out of This Device"
' App -> Storage : Pull Target Refresh Token
App -> Nginx : POST /logoutredirect
Nginx -> KC : Forward Invalidation Request
' BFF -> KC : POST /protocol/openid-connect/revoke (Revoke Token Target API)
' KC --> BFF : Invalidation Flag Synchronized Natively
KC --> Nginx : Success Response (200 OK)
Nginx --> App : Forward Success
App -> Storage : Clear Keys from Keystore
App -> User : Redirect to Login Route
@enduml